      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Bounded pass for the disclosed decorative dune/tidal abstraction, not realistic dunes/water or limestone. Similar limitations in marketing do not erase them.",
        "hardware": "Champagne/gold corner caps, central long clasp, lower circular fitting and side ring are visible. Dark teal seam is pronounced but not evidence of failed closure; no obvious gross broken hardware in supplied poses.",
        "limitations": "Frozen still-image review only; supplied technical passes were not rerun. No final user approval, photoreal equivalence, physical-phone performance, cultural authentication or continuous mechanical certification. Open disengaged latch is expected; hidden exterior lid ornament in open views is not missing. Preserve the documented pale-on-pale separation, narrow blue area, slab ends and decorative teal seam. Research is an invented sourced composition, not a surveyed coastline; UNESCO citation is a tentative listing.",
        "quality": "Pale chest, curved relief and turquoise accent remain coherent in desktop/mobile; full open silhouette and pale interior are visible. Marketing retains similarly narrow water exposure and overlapping relief.",
        "terrain": "Three shallow curved banks are visible, but smooth slab-like ends and layered plate reading persist. Blue inlay is a narrow exposed stripe/channel, especially mobile, not convincing fluid water or a geographic Khor Al Adaid reconstruction.",
        "texture": "Cloudy ivory matte surface has ambiguous stone/plaster/ceramic identity; fine limestone pores and geological realism are not resolved. Marketing adds subtle grain and edge shading without proving runtime equivalence."
      },
